      "title": "Ingersoll Rand Gears Up to Report Q3 Earnings: What's in the Offing?",
      "summary": "Ingersoll Rand is expected to report Q3 2026 revenues of $2.04 billion (up 4.5%) and adjusted EPS of 89 cents (up 3.5%), driven by segment growth and acquisition synergies. However, rising expenses and foreign currency headwinds are anticipated to pressure margins, with adjusted EBITDA margin expected to decline 120 basis points year-over-year. The company's negative Earnings ESP of -0.28% suggests limited likelihood of beating consensus estimates.",
